{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission.json\", \"summary\": \"Submitted draft/submission.json (action=research) with the map update draft/map-v6.json as the new base (base version 5): a consolidation and protection-analysis step after the fifth obligation was answered in scope. Two frontier premises are cleared because they are answered: the configuration fact's question about whether the client-visible configuration future reports the index at which the configuration was established (answered by the served check, whose artifact and check are cited) and the follower-match fact's question about whether a match recorded for a peer being removed from the latest configuration can still contribute to a commit decision before the commitment table is rebuilt. The second answer is a bounded negative reached by reading rather than execution, and it is recorded as a protection on the commitment behavior with its sources: appendConfigurationEntry appends the configuration entry, replaces the copy of the latest configuration and rebuilds the commitment table as adjacent statements on the main goroutine, and configuration changes are admitted only once the previous one is committed, so at most one is uncommitted at a time; a match landing inside that window is counted against the voter set the table still holds, and because the old and new quorum of a one-at-a-time change always intersect, any index committed there is also held by a quorum of the resulting configuration. The surface that recorded the configuration index is kept but moved from deferred to mapped against the client-contract behavior that reports it, with its reason recording what was observed and what remains; the facts and behaviors otherwise keep their assertions, identities, contexts, sources and edges, which the four clarification declarations state explicitly, including a preserved explanation for the behavior whose protection was extended.